# uv.lock is TRACKED (committed): bit-exact eval replay (invariant 7) requires a pinned
# environment — the Gate-A anchor drifted twice under floor-only pins before this was learned.

# Project runtime artifacts (content-hashed runs, data, weights).
# Root-anchored so they do NOT match the source packages src/trikaal/data/ or tests/data/.
/runs/
/data/
/raw/
/processed/
/wandb/
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.parquet
*.npy

# Local reference notes containing third-party paper text (not our own paraphrase,
# not redistributed). Kept on disk for reference, untracked to keep the public repo clean.
/docs/kronos doc summary.md

# Rented-box artifact pulls (checkpoints, ~1.7 GB). Evidence, never source.
runs_cloud/

# Demo build output — regenerate with scripts/m6_demo_build.py (refuses without a PASSING
# acceptance receipt). The 72 KB page embeds real forecasts; the RECEIPTS are what we version.
demo/index.html

# CSV dashboard is a server, not a build — nothing to version but the code and its tests.

# The manuscript was removed from the repository on 2026-08-19 by operator decision (60 files).
# Ignored so a local build tree cannot silently re-enter; the paper is distributed as a PDF.
paper/

# Local editor/tooling configuration is excluded per-clone via .git/info/exclude,
# not here — naming those directories in a tracked file publishes what it is meant to hide.
